    <section id="educational-opportunities">
        <h2>Providing Educational Opportunities</h2>
        <p>
            As a program, <abbr>FIRST</abbr> is all about educating the members of each team. Team 6324 takes this
            emphasis to heart, and thus it is our top priority. Students work with our program to develop a number of
            professional and technical skills and have the following opportunities:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Work with local engineers and professionals</li>
            <li>
                Develop skills relating to all aspects of industry, including traditional engineering and
                non-engineering skill sets.
            </li>
            <li>
                Learn to use professional tools and software such as advanced manufacturing techniques, solid modeling,
                programming and automation, photography and image editing, project management, etc.
            </li>
            <li>Develop professional communication skills necessary in a 21<sup>st</sup> century economy.</li>
            <li>Gain access to our community partner networks for further education through internships.</li>
            <li>
                Qualify for over $80 million in education scholarships that are exclusively available to
                <abbr>FIRST</abbr> students.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <section id="investing-stem">
        <h2>Investing in public <abbr>STEM</abbr> Education</h2>
        <p>
            Not only do we educate the students on our team and build, we invest in our community. Not only do we
            support all levels of <abbr>FIRST</abbr> around us, but we also promote other youth programs in Salem,
            alongside general promotion of <abbr>STEM</abbr> education. We also educate the broader community about the
            benefits of <abbr>STEM</abbr> and <abbr>FIRST</abbr> through public outreach.
        </p>
    </section>
    <section id="visibility">
        <h2>Visibility</h2>
        <p>
            Our team's visibility to the public is one of our key organizational goals. Our team participates in a
            multitude of programs and public outreach opportunities where we make ourselves and our supporters seen.
            These include, but are not limited to:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Supporting <abbr>FIRST</abbr> Lego League&reg; (<abbr>FLL</abbr>) teams in local elementary and middle
                schools.
            </li>
            <li>
                Running demonstrations at community events in Salem, such as the annual Salem Scramble, the town's
                Halloween Party, the town's annual Holiday Parade, Salembration, and others.
            </li>
            <li>
                Providing resources for neighboring teams such as machining services and facilitating a regional
                practice field in partnership with <abbr>FRC</abbr> 3467
                <a href="http://team3467.org/" target="_blank">Windham Windup</a> and
                <a href="https://https://www.canobielaketoyota.com/">Canobie Lake Toyota</a>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <section id="company-future">
        <h2>Investing in <em>Your</em> Future</h2>
        <p>
            Not only does donating to our team help the next generation of technical workers, but it can be a strong
            investment in your future. The US Bureau of Labor Statistics projects the US labor market to grow by over
            <a target="_blank" href="https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ecopro.nr0.htm">5 million jobs</a> by 2034. Our
            program and <abbr>FIRST</abbr> are at the forefront of helping our students develop the technical and
            professional skills that they will need to fill these new positions and ultimately preparing them for their
            careers and lives after graduation. You can directly support our efforts in preparing the next generation of
            engineers and technical experts.
            <br />
            How does this affect you? Well, this investment doesn't solely exist in the abstract: Of our alumni, over
            <var>&frac23;</var> stay local to New England, pursuing educational opportunities and beginning their
            careers in the New Hampshire and the Northern/Central New England area. Of that group, nearly all students
            who pursued an internship with one of our sponsors while they were attending SHS are still working with them
            or plan to begin their careers with that company.
        </p>
    </section>
    <section id="ways-to-donate">
        <h1>Ways to Donate</h1>
        <div>
            <section>
                <h2>Materials</h2>
                <p>
                    Material costs are one of our largest expenses each year. In producing a high-quality robot, we
                    typically use thousands of dollars in aluminum, structural plastics, fasteners, and electronics.
                    Directly supplying these materials via in-kind donations helps us reduce our annual supply budget.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section>
                <h2>Money</h2>
                <p>
                    Monetary donations are the most flexible way of supporting our program. We give our sponsors the
                    choice to divert funds to a specific aspect of our budget to items such as registration costs,
                    robot construction budget, travel expenses, and apparel. Every dollar helps to reduce the cost to
                    our students.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section>
                <h2>Mentoring</h2>
                <p>
                    Become a mentor! We are always looking for professionals interested in working directly with our
                    students either in-person at our meetings or at job sites through internships. We are actively
                    recruiting mentors for design, fabrication, software development, and public relations.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section id="benefits">
        <h1>Benefits</h1>
        <p>
            Beyond supporting the next generation of engineers, scientists, and business professionals, sponsors receive
            significant exposure through team media and promotional materials. Depending on the donation level, this
            includes acknowledgment on:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><p>This website</p></li>
            <li><p>Our technical binders and pit banners</p></li>
            <li><p>Our annual robot</p></li>
            <li><p>Team apparel</p></li>
            <li><p>Any additional promotional materials we create</p></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Your company's name and logo will be showcased at a number of regionally recognized events and visible to
            both students and industry professionals.
        </p>
    </section>
